### User API Testing
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### 1. Create a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

###

### 2. Create another user
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Smith",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass456!"
}

###

### 3. Try to create user with duplicate email (Should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

###

### 4. Get all users (Need JWT - will work after auth is implemented)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN

###

### 5. Get user by ID (Need JWT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/USER_ID
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN

###

### 6. Update user (Need JWT)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/USER_ID
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Updated"
}

###

### 7. Soft delete user (Need JWT)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/USER_ID
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN

###

### 8. Get user stats (Need JWT - after auth)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/stats/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN
